34,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"The inns have such strict times for eating! And we'd all be in one big room on futons, which sounds like a giant sleepover! But the all-in meal rates might be a bit unfair for some.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The offshore houses are priced per building, which is around 5,400 yen per person per night, but food is extra. I'm also concerned that all-in rates might not be the most transparent way to handle costs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It's interesting that last year some of us barely saw each other during the day. I also found that when we stayed in a shared house, it was actually quite hard to find a moment of peace alone.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The ferry schedule is quite restrictive, meaning we'd lose two full days just to travel. In contrast, the city options allow for much more flexibility since trains run every few minutes.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The inn baths are open late, but the island houses only have one bathroom for everyone... and the water might get cold. Also, the inn has very strict mealtimes and we'd all be in one room.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, if the houses are per building, does that mean we just split the total? I'm worried that if we do all-in meals, some people might pay for food they didn't even eat!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Yes, we would split the total for the house. Regarding the meals, that is exactly my concern; all-in rates can be imprecise and unfair depending on how much each person actually eats.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Sakura, @Victoria, I agree that fairness is important. But I'm also thinking about our time together. If we have too much freedom, we might end up like last year, barely seeing each other until dinner.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, flexibility doesn't have to mean isolation. However, the travel time for the island is a significant drain. If we spend two days just moving, we'll be exhausted before the trip even begins.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Toshio about the exhaustion. And if we're all in one room on futons, it might be hard to... well, it might be a bit overwhelming for some of us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"A giant sleepover sounds so fun, but I get what Daisuke means! Maybe a city place with doors would be better? But wait, if we split a house total, is that easier for the money part?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"Splitting a house total is more predictable, as the cost is fixed regardless of our individual habits. It avoids the uncertainty of paying for meals in installments or through unfair all-in packages.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"If we go with a city option, we could have the best of both worlds: a place where we can gather, but also the ability to step out for a bit of quiet if we need it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The city option is the most efficient. We avoid the rigid ferry schedules and the risk of being stranded by a bus that stops running at seven. It maximizes our actual vacation time.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I think the city option sounds safest. Having a door and no strict timetable for meals... it would be much easier to handle. I don't think I could deal with the island's bathroom situation.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'm starting to think the city is the way to go! It sounds way less stressful for Daisuke and Toshio, and we can still have our fun. Plus, paying for our own meals seems the fairest!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. A city option provides the most transparency for our budget and the most comfort for everyone. If we can determine the total accommodation cost upfront, it removes the financial uncertainty I'm worried about.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'm glad we're finding a balance. A city stay seems to solve the problem of feeling too crowded while ensuring we don't drift apart like last year. It sounds like a wonderful compromise for everyone.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we have reached a consensus. The city option minimizes wasted time and logistical stress, which is my primary concern. I am in favor of this choice.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm glad everyone is okay with the city. It feels like the most... comfortable choice for all of us. I'll be much more relaxed knowing there's a bit more privacy and flexibility.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
